  "auto.f0397ac0": "The most popular route — strong scenery, good acclimatization profile, moderately busy camps. From $2,150.",
  "auto.d4bceceb": "Longer approach through pristine forest, the highest summit success rate of any route. From $2,650.",
  "auto.b80887d5": "The only route with hut accommodation instead of tents — shorter, but a lower success rate given the pace. From $1,890.",
  "auto.9a70c424": "Rongai",
  "auto.f3a46518": "Approaches from the drier northern side — good in the rainy season, fewer crowds. From $2,200.",
  "auto.0e4bbc24": "Umbwe",
  "auto.bdcda9ee": "The steepest, most direct route — best suited to experienced trekkers with prior altitude exposure. From $2,050.",
  "auto.3b71c5a4": "9 days",
  "auto.bf8b8407": "The longest route, circling the mountain's quiet northern slopes for maximum acclimatization time. From $2,980.",
  "auto.6c8d0e16": "6 days",
  "auto.c8d3f6d1": "Shira",
  "auto.9e209457": "Similar to Lemosho but starting higher via vehicle — a faster start with a steeper first day. From $2,100.",
  "auto.51a9cb28": "KILIMANJARO PORTERS ASSISTANCE PROJECT",
  "auto.1e320cba": "We weigh porter loads. Every time.",
  "auto.86bde3ad": "Overloading porters is common on budget climbs and it is dangerous. Every Mihayo's climb is staffed to the KPAP-recommended weight limit, with proper gear provided or checked, and a tip structure disclosed to guests up front — not left to guesswork at the trailhead.",
  "auto.4a85eb09": "Before you commit to a route",
  "auto.ae840e95": "What's the actual success rate difference between routes?",
  "auto.d6e42171": "Roughly: Lemosho and Northern Circuit run 90%+, Machame around 85%, Rongai and Umbwe in the high 70s, and Marangu often below 70% due to its compressed acclimatization schedule. More days at altitude is the single biggest lever you control.",
  "auto.de939517": "Do I need prior mountaineering experience?",
  "auto.c15418b0": "No technical climbing is required on any standard route — it's a long, high-altitude walk. Cardiovascular fitness and a properly paced itinerary matter far more than climbing experience.",
  "auto.54b874a5": "What's included in the quoted price?",
  "auto.32bf536a": "Park fees, camping/hut fees, a certified guide and required support crew, all meals on the mountain, tents and cooking equipment, and rescue fee contributions. Personal gear rental and tips are quoted separately.",
  "auto.da9797c7": "Can I combine a climb with a safari or Zanzibar?",
  "auto.3ee4e893": "Yes — this is one of our most requested combinations. We typically recommend 2–3 rest days after the descent before starting a safari, and Zanzibar works well as a recovery stop after either.",
  "auto.78132a75": "Kilimanjaro porters carrying gear along the trail",
  "auto.0b79795d": "Introduction",
  "auto.3e68bbc6": "Mihayo's Safaris (\"we,\" \"us,\" \"our,\" or \"Company\") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you visit our website and use our services.",
